WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
FilmSub.lk — සිංහල උපසිරැසි සමඟ (Auto Sinhala Subtitles)

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.830
Out, all of you.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:07.920
This bastard's been meddling where he shouldn't!

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.930
I want you and your men

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.770
gone.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.170
And you will make this right.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.730
Wait outside.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.680
- Lord Commander... - Now!

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.210
- Lord Commander... - Leave us.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.090
What did you do?

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.380
I followed him.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.130
He took the baby into the woods, the newborn.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.470
- What business is that of yours? - No, you don't understand.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.020
He's killing them, all the boys.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.240
You know.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:15.910
Wildlings serve crueler gods than you or I.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.000
Those boys are Craster's offerings.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.620
Offerings? He's murdering his own children. He's a monster.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.130
Aye, many a time that monster has been the difference

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.540
between life and death for our rangers,

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.620
your uncle among them.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.290
We have other wars to fight out there.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:40.170
Like it or not, we need men like Craster.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.760
I...

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.520
I saw it.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.940
I saw

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.480
something take that child.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:01.610
Yeah. Whatever it was,

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.450
I daresay you'll see it again.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:09.260
Now, ready my horse.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.420
We leave at dawn.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.930
Don't lose it again.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.830
Gilly.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.740
You're leaving.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:53.410
I... I wanted to give you something.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.840
It belonged to my mother.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.840
- I can't take it. - Please.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.050
I want you to.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.600
My mother used it for sewing.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:15.770
She'd let me sit with her in her chamber while she sewed

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.030
and I'd read to her.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:23.610
My father put a stop to it when he found out.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.460
It's the only thing I have of hers.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.790
She gave it to me before I left for the Wall.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.540
You...

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.790
- You shouldn't give it away. - I'm not giving it away.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.270
I'm giving it to you.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.310
Keep it safe for me.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:46.970
Till I come back.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.660
Hodor.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.250
Hodor.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.000
Rouse Bran, will you? It's time for his lessons.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:46.500
Every night it's the same.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.320
I'm walking

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.670
and running, but...

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.540
I'm not... I'm not me.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:01.760
I'm running through the godswood, sniffing the dirt,

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.640
tasting blood in my mouth when I've made a fresh kill,

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.310
howling.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.730
Old Nan used to tell me stories

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:17.730
about magical people who could live inside stags, birds,

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.610
wolves.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.770
That's exactly what they are, Bran,

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.360
- stories. - So she was lying?

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.700
- They don't exist? - Well, they may have done.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.460
But they're gone from the world,

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.630
along with much else.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.830
These are dreams, Bran, nothing more.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.620
No, my dreams are different.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.500
Mine are true.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.000
I dreamt of my father dying.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:47.930
And Rickon had the same dream.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:50.930
What about all the dreams you had that didn't come true?

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.020
Right.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.600
This link is made of Valyrian steel.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:07.910
Only one maester in 100 wears it on his chain.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:12.370
It signifies that I have studied the higher mysteries.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.780
And all who study these mysteries try their hand at spells.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.800
I was no different.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.660
I was young.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:24.760
And what boy doesn't secretly wish for hidden powers

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:28.960
to lift him out of his dull life into a special one?

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.260
But in the end, for all my efforts,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:35.650
I got no more out of it than a thousand boys before me.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.520
Come on.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.450
All right.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:53.290
Maybe magic once was a mighty force in the world.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.500
But not anymore.

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:01.160
The dragons are gone.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.340
The giants are dead.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.500
And the Children of the Forest forgotten.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.390
Loras! Highgarden!

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.940
Get him!

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.790
Yield! I yield.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.120
Well fought. Approach.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.760
Rise. Remove your helm.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:51.480
You are all your father promised and more, my lady.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.770
I've seen Ser Loras bested once or twice,

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.000
but never quite in that fashion.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:00.030
Now, now, my love. My brother fought valiantly for you.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.580
That he did, my queen.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:06.260
But there can only be one champion.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:10.800
Brienne of Tarth, you may ask anything of me you desire.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.630
If it is within my power, it is yours.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:20.590
Your Grace, I ask the honor of a place in your Kingsguard.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.300
What?

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:25.180
I will be one of your seven, pledge my life to yours,

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:27.520
and keep you safe from all harm.

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:33.570
Done.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.400
Rise, Brienne of the Kingsguard.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.750
Your Grace, I have the honor to bring you Lady Catelyn Stark,

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:51.840
sent as an envoy by her son Robb, Lord of Winterfell.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.170
Lord of Winterfell and King in the North.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:58.430
Lady Catelyn. I'm pleased to see you.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:02.520
May I present my wife, Margaery of House Tyrell?

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:06.470
You are very welcome here, Lady Stark.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:08.390
I'm so sorry for your loss.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.360
You are most kind.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.150
My lady,

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:17.700
I swear to you I will see the Lannisters answer for your husband's murder.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:21.040
When I take King's Landing,

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.590
I'll bring you Joffrey's head.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.390
It will be enough to know that justice was done, my lord.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:37.140
Your Grace.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.890
And you should kneel when you approach the King.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:43.220
There's no need for that. Lady Stark is an honored guest.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:46.560
Has your son marched against Tywin Lannister yet?

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.820
I do not sit on my son's war councils.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.950
And if I did, I would not share his strategies with you.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.990
If Robb Stark wants a pact with us, he should come himself,

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.730
not hide behind his mother's skirts.

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:03.900
My son is fighting a war, not playing at one.

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:19.180
Don't worry, my lady.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.420
Our war is just beginning.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:36.450
- Your Grace. - Gerard.

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:39.280
- How's your foot? - Better, Your Grace.

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:41.530
They don't know their own size is all.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.160
Good man.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.700
I have 100,000 men at my command.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.990
All the might of the Stormlands and the Reach.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.910
And all of them young and bold like your Knight of Flowers?

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.000
It's a game to you, isn't it?

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.420
- I pity them. - Why?

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:01.250
Because it won't last.

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:05.140
Because they are the knights of summer and winter is coming.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:10.520
Brienne, escort Lady Catelyn to her tent.

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:14.570
- She's tired from her journey. - At once, Your Grace.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.140
- Shall I return after? - That won't be necessary.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.700
I would pray awhile. Alone.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.690
If you'll follow me, my lady.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:29.160
You fought bravely today, Lady Brienne.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.530
I fought for my king.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.450
Soon I'll fight for him on the battlefield.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.510
Die for him if I must.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.580
And, if it please you, Brienne's enough.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.560
I'm no lady.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.700
What are you doing here?

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.620
I live here.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.540
Are you angry with me, brother?

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:23.000
You lying bitch.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:25.800
It's not my fault you didn't recognize me.

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:28.890
Recognize you? How could I?

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.100
The last time I saw you...

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:35.020
you looked like a fat little boy.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:38.350
You were a fat little boy, too,

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.560
but I recognized you.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:44.480
- Why didn't you tell me? - I wanted to see who you were first.

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.740
And I did.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.610
The plans are made. It's time you heard them.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:53.710
- Father. - Father.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.410
The wolf pup has gone south

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.580
with the entirety of the Northern army at his back.

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:04.420
While he's tangling with the lion in the Westerlands,

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:07.000
the North is ripe for the taking.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.630
The ironborn will reave and pillage, as it was in the old days,

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.010
all along the northern coast.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.930
We'll spread our dominion across the green lands,

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.810
securing the Neck and everything above.

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:21.700
Every stronghold will yield to us, one by one.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:24.610
Winterfell may defy us for a year, but what of it?

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:29.580
The rest shall be ours, forest, field, and hall.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.960
Yara, my daughter, you'll take 30 longships

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.830
to attack Deepwood Motte.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.090
I've always wanted a castle.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.540
And what's my role in all this?

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:48.850
You'll take a ship to raid the fishing villages on the Stoney Shore.

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:50.600
A ship?

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.670
You give her 30 and I get one?

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:56.150
The Sea Bitch. We thought she'd be perfect for you.

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:02.230
- I'm to fight fishermen? - Be careful of their nets.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:09.400
Father, I fought with Robb Stark. I know his men.

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:12.650
- He won't give up the North so easily. - They won't even know we're there

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.500
- until it's too late. - What do you know of it, woman?

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.950
I'm a proven warrior.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.370
Your brothers were warriors, both of them dead

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.960
at the hands of those you seem so eager to protect.

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:28.800
I'm not protecting anyone. I just wonder if it's not wiser to wait.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:32.430
Why risk going against the North if they would be our allies?

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.230
Rise up against them and they could destroy us.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.810
But if we pledge fealty to them,

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:39.640
they'll give us Casterly Rock.

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.560
What are our words?

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:44.740
Our words?

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:50.190
- We do not sow. - We do not sow.

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:54.650
We are ironborn. We're not subjects. We're not slaves.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.710
We do not plow the fields or toil in the mine.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.870
We take what is ours.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:04.210
Your time with the wolves has made you weak.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:10.750
You act as if I volunteered to go.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.050
You gave me away, if you remember.

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.550
The day you bent the knee to Robert Baratheon.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.550
After he crushed you.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.810
Did you take what was yours then?

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.440
You gave me away!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.020
Your boy!

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:31.120
Your last boy!

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:35.750
You gave me away like I was some dog you didn't want anymore.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.950
And now you curse me because I've come home.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:52.420
You'd have our father bow down to your other family?

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:54.840
I have no other family.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.550
Don't you?

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.760
Make your choice, Theon, and do it quickly.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.430
Our ships sail with or without you.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.120
You won't let me leave this room.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:20.110
- You won't let me... - Keep your voice down.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.790
Why? You think your father can hear me?

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:28.670
He's 300 miles away!

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:33.890
I don't intend for you to stay here.

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:37.260
I might be able to bring you into the castle kitchens.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.770
Again, only temporary.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:45.310
Every man who has tasted my cooking has told me what a good whore I am.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:47.610
But you wouldn't be a cook.

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:50.240
You'd pose as a scullion.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:54.150
Scullion? What is a scullion?

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:56.860
Kitchen wench.

00:19:57.030 --> 00:19:59.690
- A kitchen wench? - Yes, but...

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:03.920
Cleaning pots? Is that how my lion wants to see me?

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:06.550
Your lion wants to see you alive.

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:08.840
We've come to a dangerous place.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.830
My sister wants to hurt me. She'll look for any weakness she can find.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:15.010
She can't know about you.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:18.800
- I'm the weakness? - It's a compliment, my lady.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:22.090
How is being a weakness a compliment?

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:27.690
Language can be a bit tricky here.

00:20:28.650 --> 00:20:30.860
I'm too stupid to understand.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.150
The stupid foreign girl.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:38.860
I am not a kitchen wench.

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:06.650
When will Joffrey and Sansa be married?

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.980
Soon, darling, when the war is over.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:11.770
Mother says I'll have a new gown for the ceremony

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:13.900
and another for the feast.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:17.410
But yours will be ivory, since you're the bride.

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:23.910
The Princess just spoke to you.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.750
Pardon, Your Grace.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:30.870
I'm sure your dress will be beautiful, Myrcella.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.050
I'm counting the days until the fighting is done

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:37.750
and I can pledge my love to the King in sight of the gods.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:44.430
Is Joffrey going to kill Sansa's brother?

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:48.940
He might.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.150
Would you like that?

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:56.910
No. I don't think so.

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:02.040
Even if he does, Sansa will do her duty.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:06.040
Won't you, little dove?

00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:26.260
Come in.

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:30.970
Who are you?

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:33.850
I'm Shae, My Lady. Your new handmaiden.

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:37.520
I didn't know I needed a new handmaiden.

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:41.230
- You're not from here. - No.

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:51.160
- What are you doing? - Waiting for you to tell me what to do.

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:55.410
I shouldn't have to tell you to do things. You should just do them.

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:57.720
What things?

00:22:58.460 --> 00:23:00.170
Change my linens, wash my clothing,

00:23:00.340 --> 00:23:03.600
scrub the floor, empty my chamber pot, brush my hair.

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:14.350
- No. - You said to brush...

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:16.020
Not now.

00:23:19.110 --> 00:23:21.200
Your chamber pot is empty.

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:23.870
Clean the table.

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:31.630
Have you ever been a handmaiden before?

00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:33.280
- Yes. - For whom?

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:35.380
- Lady Zuriff. - Lady Zuriff?

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:39.580
Lady Zuriff.

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:42.790
There is no Lady Zuriff in this city.

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:45.170
She wasn't in this city.

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:47.510
I don't know how they did things in that city,

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:51.980
but in this city, handmaidens wait on ladies, not the other way around.

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:54.890
And I don't have time to answer a thousand questions

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:57.390
and teach you how to do your job.

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:02.610
Do you want me to leave?

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:12.160
Just brush my hair.

00:24:27.760 --> 00:24:29.340
Thank the gods.

00:24:29.510 --> 00:24:31.680
I haven't had a proper shit in six days.

00:24:32.510 --> 00:24:34.590
I've encountered this problem before, my lord.

00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:37.480
The stresses of power often have this

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:40.310
insalubrious effect.

00:24:40.480 --> 00:24:43.100
Two drops with water, daily.

00:24:43.820 --> 00:24:48.290
Right. I'm so grateful to have a man of your vast knowledge and wisdom on my side.

00:24:48.450 --> 00:24:50.960
- Please. - Thank you, my lord.

00:24:56.290 --> 00:24:59.670
- I can trust you, Pycelle, can I not? - Why, yes, of course, my lord.

00:24:59.830 --> 00:25:01.960
These are perilous times.

00:25:02.130 --> 00:25:04.390
And the crown must forge new alliances.

00:25:05.260 --> 00:25:08.640
And these alliances must often be sealed in matrimony.

00:25:09.550 --> 00:25:11.630
Matrimony, huh?

00:25:12.100 --> 00:25:13.480
Yes.

00:25:13.850 --> 00:25:17.690
I'm trusting the council with these plans, but the Queen mustn't know.

00:25:18.230 --> 00:25:20.150
We can't have her meddling in affairs

00:25:20.310 --> 00:25:23.060
that could determine the future of the realm. There's too much at stake.

00:25:23.230 --> 00:25:25.810
Yes, yes. Indeed, yes.

00:25:26.150 --> 00:25:28.480
I shall be silent as the grave.

00:25:29.660 --> 00:25:33.120
I'm brokering an alliance with House Martell of Dorne.

00:25:33.950 --> 00:25:37.160
Princess Myrcella will wed their youngest son when she comes of age,

00:25:37.330 --> 00:25:41.340
ensuring their loyalty and their army, should we need it.

00:25:41.960 --> 00:25:45.010
Myrcella sent away to Dorne?

00:25:47.340 --> 00:25:50.060
But remember, the Queen mustn't know.

00:25:52.220 --> 00:25:54.140
"The Queen mustn't know."

00:25:54.810 --> 00:25:57.480
I love conversations that begin this way.

00:25:58.520 --> 00:26:01.030
I plan to marry Princess Myrcella off

00:26:01.350 --> 00:26:03.020
to Theon Greyjoy.

00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:05.990
Theon Greyjoy?

00:26:07.070 --> 00:26:09.370
Forgive me, my lord, but how?

00:26:09.530 --> 00:26:11.990
He grew up a ward of Winterfell.

00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:14.910
- He fights for Robb Stark. - Precisely.

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:20.040
Theon's father loathes the Starks and will convince the boy to come to our side.

00:26:20.870 --> 00:26:23.540
Greyjoy can destroy the Northern army from within

00:26:23.710 --> 00:26:26.090
and we can have his father's ships.

00:26:26.380 --> 00:26:28.930
But remember, you must tell no one.

00:26:29.720 --> 00:26:32.180
Tell no one what?

00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:36.020
I plan to wed Princess Myrcella to Robin Arryn of the Vale.

00:26:37.890 --> 00:26:40.550
Lysa is not fond of me.

00:26:41.020 --> 00:26:46.610
But perhaps the promise of a royal match will convince her to let bygones be bygones.

00:26:47.020 --> 00:26:50.860
She imprisoned you. She tried to execute you.

00:26:51.030 --> 00:26:53.450
And you offer her son a princess?

00:26:54.370 --> 00:26:57.710
For men in our position, holding grudges can be

00:26:57.870 --> 00:26:59.880
an encumbrance, don't you think?

00:27:00.410 --> 00:27:03.740
And I suppose you want me to broker this agreement?

00:27:03.920 --> 00:27:05.470
Who better?

00:27:09.550 --> 00:27:13.760
Yes, I could sing this song to Lysa, if I cared to.

00:27:15.430 --> 00:27:17.110
What's in it for me?

00:27:18.760 --> 00:27:22.430
The gratitude of the people of Westeros for helping to end this war,

00:27:22.600 --> 00:27:26.850
the adoration of the King for bringing the Vale back into the fold...

00:27:28.610 --> 00:27:30.200
and Harrenhal.

00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:32.110
Harrenhal is cursed.

00:27:32.610 --> 00:27:34.690
Never took you for a superstitious man.

00:27:34.860 --> 00:27:38.450
By all means, tear it down and rebuild. You'll be able to afford it.

00:27:38.620 --> 00:27:41.460
I plan to make you Lord of the Riverlands.

00:27:43.370 --> 00:27:46.080
With a single stroke, you'd make me one of the greatest lords in the realm.

00:27:46.250 --> 00:27:49.290
You served my family well in the matter of the succession.

00:27:49.460 --> 00:27:52.420
So did Janos Slynt, and he was given Harrenhal, too.

00:27:52.590 --> 00:27:54.630
Until you snatched it away.

00:27:55.090 --> 00:27:57.710
I need you to deliver Lysa Arryn.

00:27:57.890 --> 00:27:59.940
I didn't need Janos Slynt.

00:28:02.980 --> 00:28:04.730
It's settled, then?

00:28:07.060 --> 00:28:08.390
Good.

00:28:10.900 --> 00:28:14.270
- And remember... - The Queen mustn't know.

00:28:53.480 --> 00:28:55.110
That must hurt.

00:29:05.620 --> 00:29:06.990
What?

00:29:09.040 --> 00:29:10.540
What is it?

00:29:12.250 --> 00:29:14.380
A member of the Kingsguard?

00:29:16.050 --> 00:29:18.220
As if I wasn't humiliated enough already.

00:29:20.550 --> 00:29:23.970
Brienne is a very capable warrior.

00:29:25.890 --> 00:29:27.890
And she's devoted to me.

00:29:30.150 --> 00:29:31.780
You're jealous.

00:29:33.230 --> 00:29:36.440
Jealous? Of Brienne the Beauty?

00:29:37.150 --> 00:29:38.900
Don't make me laugh.

00:29:40.570 --> 00:29:43.780
- I'll make it up to you. - No, Your Grace.

00:29:44.950 --> 00:29:46.490
Not tonight.

00:29:47.710 --> 00:29:50.340
There's another Tyrell who requires your attention.

00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:54.380
You didn't win my father's support or his army on charm alone.

00:30:07.770 --> 00:30:11.110
Your vassals are starting to snigger behind your back.

00:30:11.690 --> 00:30:14.240
Brides aren't usually virgins two weeks after their wedding night.

00:30:14.400 --> 00:30:16.360
And Margaery's a virgin?

00:30:16.980 --> 00:30:18.440
Officially.

00:30:20.030 --> 00:30:22.040
Shall I bring her to you?

00:30:48.970 --> 00:30:52.600
I should warn you, I've had quite a bit of wine.

00:30:52.770 --> 00:30:54.980
As is your right. You are a king.

00:30:57.440 --> 00:30:59.400
You look very beautiful.

00:30:59.780 --> 00:31:01.450
Thank you, Your Grace.

00:31:02.150 --> 00:31:04.570
- It's a lovely gown. - You think so?

00:31:05.820 --> 00:31:07.780
I can't decide how I like it better.

00:31:07.950 --> 00:31:09.450
This way,

00:31:09.950 --> 00:31:12.660
or this way.

00:31:19.260 --> 00:31:21.010
You certainly don't need it.

00:31:22.470 --> 00:31:27.310
Although, some say the beauty most desired

00:31:27.470 --> 00:31:29.430
is the beauty concealed.

00:31:46.120 --> 00:31:48.160
Must be the wine.

00:31:48.330 --> 00:31:50.170
Here, let me.

00:32:10.640 --> 00:32:12.070
I'm sorry.

00:32:13.230 --> 00:32:15.610
Do you want my brother to come in and help?

00:32:18.230 --> 00:32:20.190
- What? - He could get you started.

00:32:20.360 --> 00:32:21.530
I know he wouldn't mind.

00:32:21.690 --> 00:32:24.150
Or I can turn over and you can pretend I'm him.

00:32:26.740 --> 00:32:28.830
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:32:34.460 --> 00:32:37.050
There's no need for us to play games.

00:32:37.710 --> 00:32:41.050
Save your lies for court. You're going to need a lot of them.

00:32:59.100 --> 00:33:04.100
Your enemies aren't happy about us. They want to tear us apart.

00:33:04.280 --> 00:33:06.530
And the best way to stop them

00:33:07.610 --> 00:33:09.320
is to put your baby

00:33:10.620 --> 00:33:12.210
in my belly.

00:33:15.910 --> 00:33:17.830
We can try again later.

00:33:18.750 --> 00:33:22.050
You decide how you want to do it, with me, with me and Loras,

00:33:22.210 --> 00:33:24.080
however else you like.

00:33:27.420 --> 00:33:29.420
Whatever you need to do.

00:33:31.970 --> 00:33:34.090
You are a king.

00:33:43.570 --> 00:33:45.200
You monster.

00:33:46.190 --> 00:33:47.980
Myrcella is my only daughter.

00:33:48.150 --> 00:33:50.690
Do you really think I'll let you sell her like a common whore?

00:33:50.870 --> 00:33:53.910
Myrcella's a princess. Some would say she was born for this.

00:33:54.080 --> 00:33:57.750
I will not let you ship her off to Dorne as I was shipped off to Robert Baratheon.

00:33:57.910 --> 00:34:00.080
Dorne is the safest place for her.

00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:03.170
Are you mad? The Martells loathe us.

00:34:03.790 --> 00:34:05.960
That's why we need to seduce them.

00:34:06.130 --> 00:34:09.540
We're going to need their support in the war your son started.

00:34:09.720 --> 00:34:12.020
- She'll be a hostage. - A guest.

00:34:12.970 --> 00:34:15.090
You won't get away with this.

00:34:15.260 --> 00:34:18.640
You think the piece of paper Father gave you keeps you safe.

00:34:21.650 --> 00:34:23.740
Ned Stark had a piece of paper, too.

00:34:26.530 --> 00:34:28.410
- It's done, Cersei. - No.

00:34:29.400 --> 00:34:31.900
- You cannot stop it. - No!

00:34:35.410 --> 00:34:38.330
Just how safe do you think Myrcella is if this city falls?

00:34:38.500 --> 00:34:42.340
Do you want to see her raped, butchered like the Targaryen children?

00:34:42.500 --> 00:34:44.090
Make no mistake.

00:34:44.250 --> 00:34:46.790
They'll mount her pretty little head on a spike right beside yours.

00:34:46.960 --> 00:34:48.880
Get out! Get out!

00:35:51.530 --> 00:35:54.120
Theon of the House Greyjoy,

00:35:54.280 --> 00:35:57.360
you would this day consecrate your faith to the Drowned God?

00:36:05.920 --> 00:36:08.170
- I would. - Kneel.

00:36:11.710 --> 00:36:15.880
Let Theon, your servant, be born again from the sea as you were.

00:36:16.840 --> 00:36:18.670
Bless him with salt.

00:36:21.470 --> 00:36:23.390
Bless him with stone.

00:36:24.440 --> 00:36:26.280
Bless him with steel.

00:36:31.480 --> 00:36:35.480
What is dead may never die.

00:36:37.070 --> 00:36:40.280
But rises again harder and stronger.

00:36:41.450 --> 00:36:42.780
Stand.

00:37:11.770 --> 00:37:14.650
I don't appreciate being made a fool of, dwarf.

00:37:15.990 --> 00:37:20.080
If Myrcella marries the Martell boy, she can't very well marry Robin Arryn, can she?

00:37:20.240 --> 00:37:23.030
No, afraid not. Sorry about that.

00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:24.780
And Harrenhal,

00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:28.030
I suppose that's off the table as well.

00:37:28.210 --> 00:37:31.670
Yes, I fear so. Sorry about that, too.

00:37:31.840 --> 00:37:34.390
Leave me out of your next deception.

00:37:34.880 --> 00:37:38.800
That's a shame. You were to be the centerpiece of my next deception.

00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:42.470
My brother Jaime rots in a northern stockade.

00:37:42.970 --> 00:37:46.300
I would see him released. That's where you come in.

00:37:46.480 --> 00:37:48.860
Robb Stark will never release the Kingslayer.

00:37:49.020 --> 00:37:51.990
No, he won't. But his mother might.

00:37:53.360 --> 00:37:55.780
How would you like to see your beloved Cat again?

00:37:59.320 --> 00:38:01.240
- Find him? - Aye.

00:38:01.700 --> 00:38:03.420
And he has company.

00:38:04.910 --> 00:38:07.580
Filthy old stoat. Almost hate to interrupt.

00:38:07.910 --> 00:38:09.500
No, you don't.

00:38:09.750 --> 00:38:11.260
No, I don't.

00:38:18.130 --> 00:38:20.460
What is the meaning of this?

00:38:20.630 --> 00:38:22.760
No, please, please.

00:38:22.930 --> 00:38:24.980
You disappoint me, Grand Maester.

00:38:25.140 --> 00:38:27.270
I am your loyal servant.

00:38:27.430 --> 00:38:31.100
So loyal that you told the Queen about my plans to send Myrcella to Dorne.

00:38:31.270 --> 00:38:33.100
No! Never!

00:38:33.270 --> 00:38:35.480
It's a falsehood. I swear it.

00:38:35.650 --> 00:38:37.160
It wasn't me.

00:38:38.280 --> 00:38:42.120
Varys. It was Varys the Spider.

00:38:42.280 --> 00:38:46.360
See, I told Varys that I was giving the Princess to the Greyjoys.

00:38:47.040 --> 00:38:50.840
I told Littlefinger that I planned to wed her to Robin Arryn.

00:38:51.370 --> 00:38:54.460
I told no one that I was offering her to the Dornish.

00:38:55.340 --> 00:38:56.930
No one but you.

00:38:57.090 --> 00:38:59.470
The eunuch has spies everywhere.

00:38:59.630 --> 00:39:01.590
Cut off his manhood and feed it to the goats.

00:39:01.760 --> 00:39:04.430
- No, no, no. - There are no goats, halfman.

00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:06.100
Well, make do.

00:39:08.520 --> 00:39:10.770
How long have you been spying for my sister?

00:39:10.940 --> 00:39:13.690
All I did, I did for House Lannister.

00:39:13.850 --> 00:39:16.020
Always. Your lord father, ask him.

00:39:16.190 --> 00:39:19.690
I've always been his servant since the days of the Mad King.

00:39:21.740 --> 00:39:23.830
- I don't like his beard. - What?

00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:26.950
What? No. No.

00:39:30.330 --> 00:39:32.880
How many Hands have you betrayed, Pycelle?

00:39:33.040 --> 00:39:35.000
Eddard Stark? Jon Arryn?

00:39:35.170 --> 00:39:37.010
Lord Arryn, he knew.

00:39:37.170 --> 00:39:39.840
He knew the truth about the Queen.

00:39:40.170 --> 00:39:45.210
And... he planned to act, to tell King Robert.

00:39:45.390 --> 00:39:47.060
So you poisoned him?

00:39:47.350 --> 00:39:49.020
No. Never.

00:39:49.180 --> 00:39:51.800
But you let him die, made sure he succumbed.

00:39:51.980 --> 00:39:54.520
Lannister... I always served Lannister.

00:39:54.690 --> 00:39:57.280
Get him out of my sight. Throw him in one of the black cells.

00:39:57.440 --> 00:39:59.070
No. No, no, no. No, please.

00:39:59.230 --> 00:40:01.190
Don't! You can't do this to me!

00:40:02.740 --> 00:40:04.290
For your trouble.

00:40:28.800 --> 00:40:31.010
You'll be pleased to know our mutual friend

00:40:31.180 --> 00:40:34.050
is doing quite well in Lady Sansa's service.

00:40:34.980 --> 00:40:37.780
Good. One of my better ideas.

00:40:37.940 --> 00:40:42.240
And it seems the Grand Maester has found his way into a black cell?

00:40:44.780 --> 00:40:46.910
Well played, My Lord Hand.

00:40:48.370 --> 00:40:50.580
But should I be worried?

00:40:50.740 --> 00:40:52.700
Janos Slynt, Pycelle...

00:40:53.040 --> 00:40:55.500
The Small Council grows smaller every day.

00:40:55.660 --> 00:40:59.000
The Council has a reputation for serving past Hands poorly.

00:40:59.170 --> 00:41:01.840
I don't mean to follow Ned Stark to the grave.

00:41:02.920 --> 00:41:05.540
Power is a curious thing, my lord.

00:41:07.050 --> 00:41:10.630
- Are you fond of riddles? - Why, am I about to hear one?

00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:12.930
Three great men sit in a room.

00:41:13.100 --> 00:41:15.810
A king, a priest and a rich man.

00:41:15.980 --> 00:41:18.610
Between them stands a common sellsword.

00:41:18.770 --> 00:41:22.480
Each great man bids the sellsword kill the other two.

00:41:22.940 --> 00:41:25.270
Who lives, who dies?

00:41:26.200 --> 00:41:27.580
Depends on the sellsword.

00:41:27.740 --> 00:41:31.960
Does it? He has neither crown nor gold nor favor with the gods.

00:41:32.120 --> 00:41:34.210
He has a sword, the power of life and death.

00:41:34.370 --> 00:41:39.040
But if it's swordsmen who rule, why do we pretend kings hold all the power?

00:41:39.630 --> 00:41:43.930
When Ned Stark lost his head, who was truly responsible?

00:41:44.550 --> 00:41:48.310
Joffrey? The executioner? Or something else?

00:41:48.470 --> 00:41:50.680
I've decided I don't like riddles.

00:41:53.810 --> 00:41:57.400
Power resides where men believe it resides.

00:41:58.810 --> 00:42:02.020
It's a trick, a shadow on the wall.

00:42:03.070 --> 00:42:09.030
And a very small man can cast a very large shadow.

00:42:49.360 --> 00:42:51.320
You should be sleeping.

00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:54.530
Tomorrow's a long march.

00:42:55.530 --> 00:42:57.870
Thirty miles, if it don't piss on us.

00:42:59.540 --> 00:43:01.090
I can't sleep.

00:43:05.710 --> 00:43:07.540
I don't like the taste.

00:43:13.340 --> 00:43:16.720
You don't drink it for the flavor, to be honest.

00:43:24.770 --> 00:43:26.100
What?

00:43:27.440 --> 00:43:29.100
How do you sleep?

00:43:29.570 --> 00:43:31.620
Same as most men, I think.

00:43:32.030 --> 00:43:34.410
But you've seen things,

00:43:35.820 --> 00:43:37.450
horrible things.

00:43:38.580 --> 00:43:39.920
Aye.

00:43:41.080 --> 00:43:43.490
I've seen some pretty things, too,

00:43:43.670 --> 00:43:45.590
but not nearly so many.

00:43:47.420 --> 00:43:49.590
How do you sleep when you...

00:43:51.470 --> 00:43:55.270
When you have those things in your head?

00:43:58.010 --> 00:43:59.720
You didn't see that.

00:44:00.810 --> 00:44:04.480
I made damn sure. I close my eyes and I see them up there.

00:44:06.150 --> 00:44:07.700
All of them

00:44:08.360 --> 00:44:10.030
standing there.

00:44:11.280 --> 00:44:12.740
Joffrey,

00:44:14.820 --> 00:44:17.320
the Queen and...

00:44:19.120 --> 00:44:20.670
and my sister.

00:44:29.710 --> 00:44:33.630
You know, we've got something in common, me and you.

00:44:33.800 --> 00:44:35.390
You know that?

00:44:36.300 --> 00:44:38.010
I must have been

00:44:39.100 --> 00:44:41.480
a couple of years older than you.

00:44:43.430 --> 00:44:47.930
I saw my brother stabbed through the heart right on our doorstep.

00:44:48.110 --> 00:44:51.160
He weren't much of a villain what skewered him.

00:44:51.650 --> 00:44:53.730
Willem, the lad's name was.

00:44:55.650 --> 00:44:58.190
He ran off before anyone could spit.

00:44:59.330 --> 00:45:01.290
And I just stood there,

00:45:02.370 --> 00:45:04.380
watching my brother die.

00:45:05.870 --> 00:45:08.160
Here's the funny part.

00:45:09.170 --> 00:45:12.010
I can't picture my brother's face anymore.

00:45:13.010 --> 00:45:14.640
But Willem,

00:45:15.010 --> 00:45:17.060
he was a nice-looking boy.

00:45:19.470 --> 00:45:23.010
He had good white teeth, blue eyes,

00:45:24.310 --> 00:45:27.400
one of those dimpled chins all the girls like.

00:45:30.110 --> 00:45:32.990
I would think about him when I was working,

00:45:33.150 --> 00:45:36.190
when I was drinking, when I was having a shit.

00:45:37.360 --> 00:45:39.070
It got to the point

00:45:39.490 --> 00:45:42.570
where I would say his name every night before I went to bed.

00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:44.570
Willem. Willem.

00:45:45.330 --> 00:45:46.750
Willem.

00:45:48.040 --> 00:45:49.750
A prayer almost.

00:45:51.960 --> 00:45:53.580
Well, one day,

00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:58.390
Willem came riding back into town.

00:46:02.390 --> 00:46:07.860
I buried an ax so deep into Willem's skull they had to bury him with it.

00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:15.900
Willem's horse got me to the Wall and I've been wearing black ever since.

00:46:21.910 --> 00:46:24.540
That'll help you sleep, eh?

00:46:32.500 --> 00:46:35.500
Get up, you lazy sons of whores!

00:46:35.670 --> 00:46:37.330
Arm yourselves.

00:46:38.510 --> 00:46:40.140
- Get up. - Get up.

00:46:40.680 --> 00:46:42.140
Keep out of sight, both of you.

00:46:42.300 --> 00:46:43.550
- No, I'm not afraid. - I can fight.

00:46:43.720 --> 00:46:45.340
Keep out of sight.

00:46:46.100 --> 00:46:48.520
If things go wrong, you run.

00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:52.600
Do you hear me? You run along north and don't look back.

00:46:54.150 --> 00:46:57.450
Hey, there's men out there who want to fuck your corpses.

00:46:57.860 --> 00:46:59.730
Outside, now!

00:47:01.820 --> 00:47:03.490
Come on, move, move!

00:47:05.330 --> 00:47:06.920
Gold cloaks!

00:47:12.500 --> 00:47:14.130
Everyone out!

00:47:18.960 --> 00:47:22.130
Hey, you! Open the damn cage!

00:47:25.970 --> 00:47:27.430
Where's the bastard, crow?

00:47:27.600 --> 00:47:29.980
Got more than a few bastards here. Who's asking?

00:47:30.140 --> 00:47:33.140
Ser Amory Lorch, sworn bannerman to Lord Tywin Lannister.

00:47:33.310 --> 00:47:36.690
These men from the capital requested our assistance.

00:47:37.270 --> 00:47:39.400
Drop your weapons in the name of the King.

00:47:39.570 --> 00:47:43.490
- Now, which king would that be? - This is your last chance.

00:47:43.990 --> 00:47:48.290
In the name of King Joffrey, drop your weapons.

00:47:51.830 --> 00:47:53.620
I don't think I will.

00:47:54.040 --> 00:47:55.500
So be it.

00:47:58.920 --> 00:48:02.170
I always hated crossbows. Take too long to load.

00:48:40.380 --> 00:48:42.340
Boy, come here. Boy!

00:48:42.510 --> 00:48:45.850
- Sweet boy, help us. - Come back here!

00:48:46.010 --> 00:48:47.590
Help us, boy!

00:48:51.100 --> 00:48:53.610
A man can fight! Free us!

00:49:00.730 --> 00:49:02.560
Quick, give it to me.

00:49:03.940 --> 00:49:05.820
Give me the ax. Give me that.

00:49:15.410 --> 00:49:17.160
Put them on the wagon!

00:49:17.920 --> 00:49:19.680
There's more here. Come on.

00:49:24.840 --> 00:49:26.710
What do we have here?

00:49:28.260 --> 00:49:29.720
No!

00:49:30.300 --> 00:49:32.430
That's a fine little blade.

00:49:34.230 --> 00:49:37.360
- Maybe I'll pick my teeth with it. - I yield! I yield!

00:49:37.520 --> 00:49:39.650
Round up any survivors.
